25,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems the most successful projects are those that allow broad booking access, whereas single-wing benefits are rated poorly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings show a desperate need for general-purpose rooms, while specialist spaces sit idle. Also, off-site hiring costs for displaced rooms are significant.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"We have a surplus of online-push technicians, but the grounds and front-of-house staff are nonexistent. Bench techs are wasting time on manual ventilation checks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Comfort-based projects are slipping by a year or more. Furthermore, outdoor work is losing weeks to rain and frost.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical and ducting costs are rising sharply. Also, we have a worrying lack of reserves for replacing old audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, if general rooms are in demand, that aligns with the high ratings for bookable spaces.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, exactly. The data suggests we should prioritize flexibility over niche specialization.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, if mechanical costs are rising, we should be cautious about any heavy HVAC work.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, and if it's outdoors, the weather will likely push the deadline back.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, that makes the ""comfort"" projects you mentioned even more of a liability.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@George, you mentioned technicians doing manual routines. Is that due to equipment failure?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, does the delivery slip apply to all non-inspection works, or just specific types?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,George,,"@Toshio, it's the extraction equipment. It's outdated and requires manual intervention.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, generally, anything argued for on ""appeal"" rather than ""necessity"" seems to suffer the most delay.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are facing a trifecta of rising mechanical costs, weather delays, and staffing gaps.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
