50,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"The candidates are A: Lab Ventilation, B: Study Commons, C: Path Network, and D: Media Center. I lean toward B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Victoria,,B solves the general room shortage and avoids the off-site hiring costs associated with long closures.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,George,,"A would relieve the bench technicians, but Benjamin mentioned mechanical costs are spiking. B is safer.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"C is exposed to weather and B is ""comfort-based,"" but D's AV kit might lack the renewal reserves Benjamin found.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,D is a risk due to the AV reserves. C is a risk due to tender costs and weather. B is the most stable.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, if B is ""comfort-based,"" do you think it will slip by a year?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, perhaps, but the demand for general study space is a functional necessity now, not just a luxury.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, would the Study Commons require significant mechanical work?","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, it might, but it's indoors, so we avoid the weather days I saw in the diaries.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, a conversion of a hall is mostly fit-out, not heavy plant. It's much cheaper than A.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Toshio,,B also fits the profile of the highest-rated post-occupancy projects because it's bookable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. It addresses the booking data gaps perfectly.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,George,,I can support B. It doesn't add to the burden of the missing grounds staff like C would.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we can frame it as a necessity for student capacity, we might avoid the delivery slips.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logically, B has the fewest financial and environmental red flags.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
